      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "ITERATIVE EDITING — build the image in passes, like a real studio process.\n\nStage 1 generates clean line art. Stage 2 edits it (add color). Stage 3 edits the RESULT of stage 2 (add an element). Each Editor feeds the next, and each stage is saved so you can compare.\n\nWHY CHAIN INSTEAD OF ONE GIANT PROMPT? One change per pass keeps control: if stage 3 goes wrong, stages 1-2 are safe and you only redo the last step. It's underdrawing -> color -> detail.\n\nWHAT COMPOUNDS: each edit re-interprets the whole image, so tiny drifts accumulate — after many passes, edges soften and details mutate. When drift gets objectionable, that's the signal to stop iterating (or restart from an earlier stage).\n\nEXERCISE: plan a 3-pass painting before you run anything — write the three prompts first. Painters call this a study; here it's also cheaper."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
